WHY THIS IS DELIBERATE

Withholding a licence keeps every option open while the project is private
(CLAUDE.md section 4.2, decision D2). As sole copyright holder, the author
can relicense this code under any terms later -- permissive, copyleft, or
commercial. Publishing under an open-source licence first is a one-way
door for any contribution that is not the author's own, which is why D2
also records that external pull requests are not accepted without a CLA.

Revisit this file when the repository goes public, which D2 schedules for
after M4.


THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

This software links the Qt framework, used under the GNU Lesser General
Public License version 3 (LGPLv3). Only LGPL-available Qt modules are used;
GPL-only modules such as QtCharts and QtDataVisualization are excluded by
design (CLAUDE.md constraint L1), which is why charts here are hand-built.

Qt is linked dynamically and is not modified. LGPLv3 obligations -- shipping
the licence text, naming the linked Qt version, and allowing a recipient to
relink against their own build of Qt -- attach to distributed binaries, not
to this source repository. They must be satisfied before any release
artifact (AppImage, APK) is published.

The test suite uses Catch2, under the Boost Software License 1.0. It is a
build-time dependency only and is not distributed with the application.
